EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 OF 3 LYMPH NODES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left sentinel node count  REMOVED_CASE_ID    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of fibrofatty tissue which is dissected to reveal a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm potential lymph node which is frozen entirely as FX 1  now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the tissue is now submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  stitch at axillary tail   is a 345 gram  25 x 15 x 3 4cm left mastectomy specimen with a single stitch marking the axillary tail  There is a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm containing the nipple  The surface of the skin is tan and without any puckering or retractions  The anterior resection margin is dark yellow red and fatty  Located 2 4cm superior to the skin ellipse and 5 0cm inferior to the superior most margin is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm cavity open to the anterior aspect which extends 1 5cm deep into the breast tissue  The posterior surface is yellow  smooth and glistening  The anterior surface is inked blue  the posterior surface is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal yellow white fibrofatty breast tissue  Around the area of the cavity  the breast tissue is hemorrhagic and slightly firm  Posterior and medial to the cavity there is an irregularly shaped region of abnormally firm tissue that is 6cm wide by approximately 3cm in diameter  The tissue in this region is heterogeneous  with white areas mixed with pink gray areas  This abnormal area comes to within 0 4cm of the posterior margin  and is greater 2cm from all other margins  The remainder of the breast tissue contains scattered brown fluid filled cysts  The axillary tail aspect is dissected to reveal no identifiable lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic cavity with respect to posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Hemorrhagic cavity with respect to anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional representative sections of the cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the ill defined abnormally firm area  tumor   including nearest margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of breast tissue away from the cavity and tumor   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of breast tissue containing brown fluid filled cyst   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the axillary tail   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nipple  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Subareolar tissue  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue superior medial to nipple  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Subareolar fibrocystic changes  Also received in the same container is a 20cm in circumference  0 6cm in width donut shaped piece of skin  The surface of the skin is tan pink and unremarkable  the deep resection margin is dark red  and unremarkable  The deep resection margin is inked black  A representative section of this skin is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  non sentinel tissue left breast   is an aggregate of fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  Out of the fat are dissected 5 potential lymph nodes ranging in size from 1 4cm in greatest dimension to 0 4cm in greatest diameter  The largest lymph node is bisected and submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining lymph nodes are submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the fatty tissue is submitted in toto as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SEC