Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 12 CLINICAL DATA  Palpable left breast lesion in upper inner quadrant and lateral left breast lesion on mammogram                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT MEDIAL   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  WITHIN REMOVED_DATE MM OF AN INKED MARGIN AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    CRIBRIFORM AND COMEDO TYPE PRESENT AT AN INKED CAUTERIZED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  1   NOTE  1  The carcinoma measures 1 1cm in greatest histological dimension  Vascular invasion is not identified  2  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  3  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  4  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  BREAST  LEFT LATERAL   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  PRESENT AT AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2   CRIBRIFORM TYPE WITH CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES AND PRESENT AT THE INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2   NOTE  2  The carcinoma measures 0 7cm in greatest histological dimension  The ductal carcinoma in situ is present within and adjacent to the infiltrating carcinoma  Vascular invasion is not identified  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FIBROSIS  MICROCYST FORMATION  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  AND APOCRINE METAPLASIA  3  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 20 58 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL AND LATERAL MASSES   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 15     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two specimens  Labeled  left breast  medial  palpable lesion   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm fibroadipose tissue fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal a fatty cut surface with white fibrous tissue  but no areas suspicious for carcinoma  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through E  Labeled  left breast  lateral lesion   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibroadipose tissue fragment  inked and sectioned to reveal a fatty cut surface with areas of white  rubbery  shiny tissue  Fragment is entirely submitted in F through L  Resident  DARRYL E  PAL