Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 29 CLINICAL DATA  32 year old who had a right breast biopsy which showed a grade 3 invasive ductal carcinoma extending to a margin of the specimen                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY SITE AND REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST  DEEP  MARGIN  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  THREE DUCT PROFILES  SPANNING A REGION THAT IS REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  MEASURED FROM SLIDES   EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE BIOPSY SITE  WITH ONE FOCUS THAT IS REMOVED_DATE CM FROM A DEEP MARGIN  NOTE  No definite lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 19 OF 19 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 15                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 40 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are two containers each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  and unit number  Specimen  1 consists of a breast biopsy with an adherent skin ellipse  The biopsy measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Within the skin ellipse is a healing surgical incisional scar  1 5cm in length  The specimen has been oriented as stated on the container  long suture lateral  and short suture  superior  The specimen has been painted in the following manner  Lateral margin green Medial margin blue Anterior and deep surgical resection margins   black ink  The specimen has been sectioned at 0 5cm intervals and reveals a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm  A portion of the biopsy cavity closest to the deep surgical resection margin shows a small focus  0 5 x 0 5cm   of firm  tan tissue suspicious for carcinoma  This area is located 1 2cm from the nearest deep inked surgical resection margin  The biopsy cavity is continuous with the overlying adherent skin ellipse and healing surgical scar  The biopsy cavity comes to within 1 5cm of the medial inked margin and 1 8cm from the lateral inked surgical resection margin  The skin ellipse shows unremarkable tan  wrinkled tissue with no other abnormalities other than the surgical incision  Sections from this specimen will be submitted as follows  A  medial inked surgical resection margins  blue  B  lateral surgical resection margins  green  C  superior surgical resection margins  black  D G  sections through a biopsy cavity  DandE  show closest approximation to deep inked surgical resection margin                     A shows biopsy cavity in closest approximation to overlying skin ellipse   H  representative section through firm area of breast near medial surgical resection margin  grossly not tumor The second specimen consists of a portion of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  Lymph nodes are identified within this specimen  The largest lymph node measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Representative sections of the nodes will be submitted in the following cassettes  I  representative sections from 3 nodes J  5 nodes K  5 nodes L  3 nodes M  3 nodes N  nodes Resident  SUSAN TEBBUTT  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Ruth B Felsen  M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT  PART B  AXILLARY CONTENTS  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 15 50 CLINICAL DATA  Local recurrence high grade DCIS                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  ADJACENT TO THE BIOPSY SITE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  BEAST  LEFT   SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 15 39                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 50     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    The lymph node does not contain keratin positive carcinoma cells  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 15 38 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  lymph node  left axilla  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm portion of adipose tissue which contains a single REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan brown lymph node  The lymph node is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved left breast  are multiple  irregular fragments of focally cauterized fibroadipose tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  Sectioning through the tissue reveals predominantly yellow  fatty cut surfaces with a small amount of fibrous tissue  The specimen has been previously infused with blue dye  No lesions or masses are grossly appreciated or palpated  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes B through E  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast re excision  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm portion of fibroadipose breast tissue with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm tan white skin ellipse  The skin ellipse has a central  2 3cm healing surgical scar  There is a short suture designating the superior margin and a long suture designating the lateral margin  The specimen has been previously infused with blue dye  The specimen is entirely inked black and the deep margin is overinked in blue  Sectioning through the specimen reveals no discrete biopsy cavity  however  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm area which on sectioning shows fibrous tissue with focal areas of surrounding fat necrosis  This area is located 0 3cm from the superior margin  2 3cm from the deep margin  0 5cm from the inferior margin  and 0 6cm from the overlying skin ellipse  anterior margin   The remainder of the specimen is heavily infused with blue dye but with no other discrete lesions or masses  SECTION CODE F G  Inked margins  H I  Superior margin  J K  Inferior margin  L M  Anterior margin with skin  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE   LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART B  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL MARGIN  EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION , Unchecked.
