nd eosin stained section  other immunostained sections  or still deeper sections that were subsequently obtained  Adjacent to this focus of microinvasive carcinoma is a second focus of ductal carcinoma in situ that is grade 1  A topographically separate second focus of ductal carcinoma in situ in the same section is grade 3  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  Wyatt  REMOVE_MRN and  left breast   is a 21 x 20 x 3cm oriented left simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch designating axillary portion of the specimen  The anterior surface bears a 19 x 6cm tan brown skin ellipse  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm nipple which are grossly unremarkable  There is a 2 5cm linear well healed scar present approximately between 1 and 3 o clock position  3cm from the areola in the outer quadrant  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially bread loafed to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 5cm fibrotic  calcified scar approximately between 1 and 3 o clock position in the outer quadrant beneath the overlying linear well healed scar on skin which lies 0 3cm from posterior and 2 4cm from overlying margin  Approximately 7cm medial to this scar there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm biopsy cavity approximately between 6 and 7 o clock position  The biopsy cavity is lined a glistening lining and contain hemorrhagic material and a clip  The biopsy cavity lies 0 6cm from posterior and 5cm from overlying anterior inked margin  The breast parenchyma between the scar and the biopsy cavity contains predominantly tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue interspersed with a moderate amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma contains a moderate amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue admixed with tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No additional discrete mass or lesion is grossly appreciated  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpate