ared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 10 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right breast   are two fragments of breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  The larger fragment contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm tan white  granular  ill defined firm mass  0 25cm from the inked resection margin  The remainder of both fragments are unremarkable  A section of tumor is frozen as FX 1  and resubmitted in cassette A  Additional sections of the tumor are submitted in B D  Two sections of the small fragment are submitted in cassettes E and F  A small portion of specimen was taken for research at Dr  Sgroi s lab  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   