Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 MAY 93 at 15 40 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY   INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor grows with an unusual pattern that makes it difficult to determine the proportions of in situ and invasive carcinoma  Blood vessel or lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The tumor shows staining for chromogranin and synaptophysin  which indicates neuroendocrine differentiation  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 MAY 93 at 16 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 93 at 13 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Sectioning reveals a 0 8cm in diameter  irregularly shaped  firm  tan lesion abutting an inked margin  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  The lesion is too small for biochemical estrogen receptor study  The remainder is submitted entirely in B through E  Resident  George O  Kucyj  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT   BIOPSY  CARCINOMA  PROBABLY INFILTRATING  AWAIT PERMANENTS   O R  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 04  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Aleksandr Vasilyev  M D  Reports To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  WILLIAM GERALD AUSTEN  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Right simple mastectomy  IDC with close margin  status post lymph node dissection FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  FOUR MICROSCOPIC FOCI  0 5  REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE AND REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT ADJACENT TO THE HEALING BIOPSY SITE AND PRESET IN 3 OF 10 TISSUE BLOCKS   SEE NOTE   RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU PRESENT IN 4 OF 10 TISSUE BLOCKS  NOTE  The margins of resection are free of in situ and invasive carcinoma  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with a stitch attached to the lateral edge and a 2 5cm fragment of skin at the inferior surface with areola intact nipple complex  The anterior surface is inked blue  the posterior surface is inked black  the inferior surface is inked yellow and the superior surface is inked green  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity underlying the nipple and extending towards the 9 o clock  The cavity extends to within 0 2cm from the anterior resection margin and 1 4cm from the posterior resection margin  It is greater than 5 0cm from the lateral and roughly about 4 0cm from the superior resection margin  There is a separate 0 5cm hard nodule superior to the biopsy cavity that lies within 1 9cm from the superior resection margin  2 3cm from the posterior resection margin and roughly 1 2cm from the anterior resection margin  The nodule is hard with tan  homogeneous cut surface  The rest of the breast tissue shows diffuse fibrocystic change most prominent at the lateral aspect of the specimen  No lymph nodes identified  The biopsy cavity is submitted representatively as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The nodule is submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Two representative sections of the uninvolved breast are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   An additional section of the biopsy cavity is submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Aleksandr Vasilyev M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
