Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 12 02 CLINICAL DATA  50 year old with right breast mass  no calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE 1  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  WITH FOCAL FLORID EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL LUTEAL CHANGES  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  gross measurement   Grade  1 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  Invasive carcinoma extends to less than 0 2cm from the inked margin of the specimen in foci  Stains for receptors  Requested  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 18 37                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block C   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm unoriented fibrofatty breast tissue fragment  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned displaying an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm indurated mass which grossly abuts the inked margin  The specimen is submitted in its entirety sequentially in cassettes A J with the lesion in cassettes B D  Gross Description by  JAMES BARRY Resident  TAI YUAN LIN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 08 CLINICAL DATA  2cm mass left breast  non palpable                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  CONSISTENT WITH PHYLLOIDES TUMOR  Diagnosis by  Julie Fanburg  MD Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 12 30 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  are fragments  5  of a needle biopsy specimen consisting of white firm tissue and adipose tissue and which range in size from 0 3cm in length to 0 8cm in length  The entire specimen is submitted in cassette A  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Perry James Culver  M D  Daniel Benjamin Kopans  M D  PART   BREAST CORE BIOPSY  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  21 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  21 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 11 47 CLINICAL DATA  Bilateral breast mass with FNA suggestions of lymphoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  DIFFUSE LARGE B CELL LYMPHOMA  SMALL FOCI  PROBABLY ARISING FROM A LOW GRADE B CELL LYMPHOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  This case is unusual and is difficult to subclassify precisely  There is a dense nodular and diffuse lymphoid infiltrate  forming an ill defined mass and extensively involving the surrounding fat  The nodules vary in size and appear to have a lobular arrangement  consisting of peri acinar periductal proliferation of small lymphocytes admixed with many scattered transformed large lymphocytes  Some smaller nodules are vaguely defined and are composed of dense small to medium sized lymphocytes  some with descinable pale cytoplasm  Between nodules and in fat are large non cleaved lymphocytes in clusters or occasionally in sheets with admixed medium sized or small cells  Monotonous populations that are typical of centrocytes or marginal zone cells are not seen  Definitive follicular structures are not an obvious histologic feature  On morphologic grounds  the number of large atypical lymphocytes infiltrating the tissue is consistent  at least focally  with a diagnosis of large cell lymphoma  The lymphoid proliferation with singly distributed large cell component in many areas suggests that the large cell lymphoma may be associated with a low grade lymphoma  Immunoperoxidase stains on the paraffin section show that large cells are  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     confirming the diagnosis of diffuse large B cell lymphoma  However  The B cells are  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   arguing against the presence of a follicular or mantle cell lymphoma  see addendum   Although the extranodal location  the intimate association of lymphoid infiltrate with breast lobules and lack of large cell sheeting out tend to imply a lymphoma of mucosa associated lymphoid tissue  MALT  type  the histomorphology and immunophenotype are non specific and not sufficient to definitively subclassify the low grade component  Dr  Judith A  Ferry has reviewed the case the concurs with the diagnosis  Diagnosis by  HENRY DONG  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 07 58                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS  FROZEN AND PARAFFIN SECTIONS  HP  REMOVED_CASE_ID    With antibodies to immunoglobulin there is a suggestion of monotypic  IgM Lambda  staining of many lymphoid cells in nodular and diffuse patterns  With antibodies to B lineage antigen s    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of most large cells and many small to medium sized cells  The B cells are negative for antibodies to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Large cells are positive for Bcl 2  With antibody to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   there is staining of dendritic pattern within some small nodules  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results support the diagnosis of a B cell lymphoma and argue against mantle and follicular lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  HENRY DONG  MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 23 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is unoriented fragment of yellow soft tissue  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal fatty tissue with a tan white nodular cut surface  A representative section is frozen as fx 1 and the frozen tissue is saved  Another section adjacent to frozen section  1 is fixed in B 5  and now submitted in cassette F  The remaining tissue is entirely submitted in cassette A E  Gross Description by  MANCONG ZHANG  MD Resident  VIKRAM DESHPANDE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 LEFT  BREAST  HIGHLY ATYPICAL LYMPHOID INFILTRATE  CONSISTENT WITH MIXED SMALL CELL LARGE CELL MALIGNANT LYMPHOMA  O R  Resident  MANCONG ZHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  PART   BREAST LEFT  EXCISION , Unchecked.
