Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 54 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   NEEDLE BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   Tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 93 at 13 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin are four soft  tan yellow to tan pink cores of tissue  ranging from 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  submitted entirely in A  Gross Description by  John Allick Resident  Andrea Flieder  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST TISSUE   report_end  , Unchecked.
