ve for lymphatic invasion in this specimen part       F  BREAST EXCISION  RIGHT MEDIAL MARGIN     Invasive ductal carcinoma  grade 2  spanning 0 8cm and broadly present at the  inked margin     Focal lymphatic invasion  See note     Ductal carcinoma in situ  present  0 1cm from the inked margin in multiple  foci     NOTE  Dr  Kristina Braaten has reviewed slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and concurs with the  diagnosis of lymphatic invasion       SYNOPTIC REPORT  Invasive Breast Carcinoma  PARTS INCLUDED  A  SPECIMEN LATERALITY  Right  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  TUMOR SIZE  2 1cm  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified in main specimen  part A    but see medial margin specimen  part F   BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  DISTANCES TO MARGINS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  INKED MARGIN  Positive  NOTE  This synoptic report does not include results of separately submitted  margins  please refer to appropriate parts of this case for those results   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Present  LOCATION  Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma  GRADE  1 and 2  DISTANCES TO MARGINS FOR DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INKED MARGIN  Positive  NOTE  This synoptic report does not include results of separately submitted  margins  please refer to appropriate parts of this case for those results   ANCILLARY STUDIES  RECEPTOR STUDIES  Requested on block s   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID       BILLING COMMENT  The resection margins of the specimens were inked and  microscopically evaluated  This case does not contain all the coding components  for CMS PQRI measure  99          Electronically Signed Out By Melinda Jean Fan Lerwill MD           By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis  certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or  corrected the diagnosis       PROCEDURES ADDENDA    Hormone Receptor Quantitation  Ordered Date  REMOVED_DATE    A  BREAST EXCISION  RIGHT   Block tested   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The invasive tumor c