g uninvolved parenchyma is predominately dense white fibrous tissue with a minimum amount of tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  There is a 0 2cm cyst located at the medial aspect which is filled with dark brown cloudy fluid  No additional discrete masses or lesions are identified  The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from the lateral to medial aspect in cassettes A J with the well circumscribed mass in cassette D E and the area denoted by the needle localization wire in cassette D G  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
