ults of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 97 at 17 04     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labelled with patients name  unit number  and   left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fibroadipose tissue fragment  The specimen margins are inked as follows  Yellow   superior  red   lateral  green   medial  blue   inferior  black   deep  Serial sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm well circumscribed  hard  tan   pink mass  0 5cm from the deep margin and 1 0cm from the superior margin  A representative portion is frozen and saved frozen  Section code AandB  Deep margin C  Superior margin DandE  Mass  representative section  br report_end  , Unchecked.
