resh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left modified radical mastectomy   is a 26 x 20 x 5 5cm left modified radical mastectomy specimen with an attached REMOVED_DATE x 7 x 3cm axillary tail  The specimen is oriented with a short stitch indicating the superior aspect and a long stitch indicating the lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is surfaced by a 23 x 10 5cm tan pink skin ellipse with a 4 x 3cm dark brown areola with an inverted nipple  Located 3cm medial to the areola is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm dark brown discoloration  consistent with a previous biopsy site that is 1 5cm to the closest skin margin  No other scars or other skin lesions are grossly appreciated  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  and the posterior resection margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm firm indurated mass that is 1 5cm to the closest posterior margin and 4 8cm to the closest anterior margin  The mass is located in the central to lower inner quadrant of the breast  and immediately anterior to the mass  there is a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of fibrous tissue  The remaining mammary tissue is fibrofatty with moderate amounts of fibrous and diffusely nodular tissue  Sectioning of the axillary tail reveals 3 candidate lymph nodes ranging in greatest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 1 5cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass to closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remaining small portion of mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire nipple to underlying breast parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire skin biopsy site to closest skin margin  radially   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of centrally located fibrous tissue to areola   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node  bisected   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph node   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  