Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 53 CLINICAL DATA  63 year old female with biopsy proven right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   PARTIAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 2 3  90   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  10   SINGLE FOCUS  COMEDO TYPE  3  BREAST ATROPHY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 11 OF 11 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Inked resection margins are free of carcinoma  the closest margin is at least 0 5cm  from tumor  There is no evidence of lymphatic or vascular invasion  Carcinoma is present in two of fifteen slides  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Leonard Atkins  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 57                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of 