Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  14 MAY 01 ACCESSIONED ON  14 MAY 01 at 16 43 CLINICAL DATA  Lobular carcinoma in the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  SENTINEL   BIOPSY  METASTATIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA  ONE NODE   SEE NOTE  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  The tumor cells are singly dispersed in minor foci within the node  and are demonstrated conclusively only on immunostains of each of three levels of block B  No cytokeratin positive cells are identified on the immunostains of three levels of block A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY  NON SENTINEL   BIOPSY  METASTATIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA  ONE NODE   WITH EXTRACAPSULAR EXTENSION  SEE NOTE  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Because the tumor is of a lobular type and the tumor cells are small and singly dispersed  at least in part  the extent of nodal involvement cannot be determined  BREAST  RIGHT   TOTAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  SEE TABLE  1 AND NOTE  FOCAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA AND A SMALL DUCT PAPILLOMA  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS 1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 7cm  Grade  2 Lymphatic vessel invasion  Not identified  Blood vessel invasion  Not identified  Margin of invasive carcinoma  The surgical margins are negative for tumor  Stains for receptors  Requested  NOTE  Tumor is extensively present on all of the submitted sections of the mastectomy  F P   including tissue away from the mass identified by gross examination  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  ADDITIONAL   BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 OF 3 NODES  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  22 MAY 01 at 18 15                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum    